    "fault_type": "label_noise",
    "onset_round": 1,
    "confidence": 0.45,
    "rationale": "Weaker case. PR's update direction disagrees with the federation median more than any other client's apart from the three poisoned clients (mean cosine 0.656, z -8.3). The disagreement is present in every round from round 1 (per-round cosines 0.37-0.89), so it is persistent rather than a transient. Its local AUC (0.714) is among the lowest, which is the pattern label noise would produce. Its CITL (0.043) and prevalence are close to the federation's, so there is no clear prevalence shift, and the norm is normal. Confidence is moderate because the AUC is only weakly distinct from several other clients.",
