  "summary": "I screened all 52 clients with the all-client views of client_updates, client_performance, drift_by_round, feature_summary and subgroup_outcomes (Sex, AgeGroup, Income), then confirmed the leads with narrower queries. Three clients (HI, SC, WI) show a clear poisoning signature: update norms about 11-15x the median and cosine about -0.97 to the median, present from round 1, with normal local performance. I report them with high confidence. PR is reported as a moderate-confidence label_noise lead: its updates persistently disagree with the federation (cosine z -8.3 from round 1) and its AUC is low, but the AUC evidence is weak. Not reported: GU, AL, DC and VI (cosine z between -3.9 and -6.1 but without corroborating performance or subgroup evidence; GU's per-round check was refused once the budget was exhausted); ND HighChol and NC GenHlth (feature outliers that disappeared on narrower re-query); and the subgroup O/E outliers (WV, SD, GU, DC, WI), which sit at noise-level z on small subgroups. No drift flags appeared for any client. The budget was fully spent (20.0 epsilon)."
